    {
      "id": "BFL-01",
      "title": "A signed carry gives the difference of two Bernoulli coefficients",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-bernoulli-carry",
      "statement": "For F>1, k=e+1≥2, b prime to F and each unit representative u, put y=[bu] and θ=2⌊bu/F⌋−(b−1). With D=2k·primorial(k+1) and C the normalized Bernoulli coefficient, D[(bu)^e θ+2(C(y)−b^kC(u))] is an integer multiple of F.",
