    {
      "id": "BFL-02",
      "title": "Summing the carries and recovering the primitive valuation",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-bernoulli-congruence",
      "statement": "For an odd prime ℓ and level F=f_{ℓ′}ℓ^m, k=e+1≥2 and a primitive character of the selected parity, let χ be its induced character at F. The signed-carry sum S satisfies D[χ(b)b^e S−2(χ(b)b^k−1)T_F]≡0 modulo ℓ^m, where T_F is the generalized Bernoulli value at F divided by k. When χ(b)b^k−1 is a unit and m meets the strict depth condition, the lifted scalar z has the same ℓ-adic norm as the primitive Bernoulli value divided by k.",
      "dependencies": [
        "BFL-01"
      ],
